{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured","id":1153948,"title":"What Happens when a Dauntain is captured?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-29T11:36:58-07:00","id":1153948,"title":"What Happens when a Dauntain is captured?","content":"wondered a bit, ever since reading the immortal eye trilogy... what happens when a dauntain is brought in chains before the nobility.<br /> <br /> Ideas think they'll be dispatched as a mercy, or given a trial to determine if they can be rehabilitated or not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T11:53:48-07:00","id":1154455,"title":"","content":"Depends on the noble. <br /> But keep in mind: Killing isn't the same to Changelings as it is to the rest of the WoD. Execution will probably done with Chimerical weapons and the mists will take care for a while (pretty long, since Dautain have really high banality).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T15:12:59-07:00","id":1154526,"title":"","content":"ideas what can be done with a Chimericly dead Enemy? Dauntain or otherwise? <br /> <br /> a Chivalrous noble, will want to keep him safe... but also keep their subjects safe from them<br /> <br /> <br /> best guess, is to assign some kinain to watch them.;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T17:13:23-07:00","id":1154550,"title":"","content":"It also might depend on the type of dauntain. I remember there is one type that sheds infected glamour. Even if he skirts changeling society and freeholds his bloody sloshed off glamour could infect chimeras and freeholds could cause quite the stir. What does a noble do when the glamour from the balefire is diseased as the one who did it lay before him?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T09:27:27-07:00","id":1154739,"title":"","content":"Are we talking about C20 Dauntain, or Autumn People Dauntain? Because I would see C20 Dauntain as being treated like Escheat breaking Changelings, while Autumn People Dauntain would be treated like horribly tainted monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:56:52-07:00","id":1154814,"title":"","content":"Warlocks can be closer to the former, tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T10:19:58-07:00","id":1155114,"title":"","content":"Based on the C20 writeup, I imagine most Dauntain would face mortal death. They're described as being &quot;among the most frightening&quot; things changelings can think of and &quot;a horror that chills straight to the soul.&quot; The book goes on to say that most changelings believe that when Dauntain are killed, they are reincarnated and given a second chance (whether or not that's true, it's what the Kithain believe). So, with all that in mind, I do think that local nobility would put Dauntain to death, if not to save themselves from the Dauntain, then to save the Dauntain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:38:02-07:00","id":1155147,"title":"","content":"I can't remember, is there a Kenning roll or something to determine if someone is a Dauntain? Naming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T01:42:01-08:00","id":1156258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured#post1153948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wondered a bit, ever since reading the immortal eye trilogy... what happens when a dauntain is brought in chains before the nobility.<br /> <br /> Ideas think they'll be dispatched as a mercy, or given a trial to determine if they can be rehabilitated or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dauntain cannot be rehabilitated as if they're criminals of society. They're monstrous mockeries, damaged by their own ancient choices or with curses inflicted on them. They are, fundamentally, broken. The Dreaming rejects them, and they're fairly twisted because of it. It's not a matter of the Escheat being broken, because the Dreaming does not recognize the Dauntain as belonging to it. They're traumatized, damaged children rejected by the gestational force that should nurture them, and while some of them believe they can be &quot;cured&quot;, none of them ever are and life after life, they come back with that punishment literally branded on them. <br /> <br /> A changeling can absolutely get away with full on mortal death and/or permanent Undoing. The Dreaming specifically rejects the Dauntain; the Escheat and the Old Laws\u2122 might be enforced socially or politically, but mystically? The Dreaming wants the Dauntain gone from it, and does not punish those who remove the pestilence. Beyond that? Sweet Jesus, have you looked at Ruin? Smart Kithain wouldn't want to risk a Dauntain anywhere near their free holds for the formalities of a trial, because the one thing the Dauntain are really *really* good at is fucking up Glamour and sources of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":3785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","user":"Luka C","date":".  For clarity. 11-06-2017, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T01:43:51-08:00","id":1156259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1155147#post1155147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember, is there a Kenning roll or something to determine if someone is a Dauntain? Naming?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are literally branded, and changelings might not know what language the Brand is in, but on an instinctual level, they recognize it as a Dauntain Brand if they catch sight of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T04:35:43-08:00","id":1156282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1156259#post1156259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are literally branded, and changelings might not know what language the Brand is in, but on an instinctual level, they recognize it as a Dauntain Brand if they catch sight of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I ask why potential stories of not knowing who's a Dauntain would be closed off like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","user":"zenten","date":".  Much too harsh 11-06-2017, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T14:17:52-08:00","id":1156473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1156282#post1156282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can I ask why potential stories of not knowing who's a Dauntain would be closed off like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand: how do you feel it closes stories off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T15:14:47-08:00","id":1156496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1156473#post1156473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I understand: how do you feel it closes stories off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every story involving a Dauntain is just &quot;how do we stop this objectively evil monster that everyone agrees is a monster&quot;. No moral dilemmas, no trying to figure out who is a Dauntain, just a short battle that goes one of two ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T21:58:52-08:00","id":1156579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1156258#post1156258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dauntain cannot be rehabilitated as if they're criminals of society. They're monstrous mockeries, damaged by their own ancient choices or with curses inflicted on them. They are, fundamentally, broken. The Dreaming rejects them, and they're fairly twisted because of it. It's not a matter of the Escheat being broken, because the Dreaming does not recognize the Dauntain as belonging to it. They're traumatized, damaged children rejected by the gestational force that should nurture them, and while some of them believe they can be &quot;cured&quot;, none of them ever are and life after life, they come back with that punishment literally branded on them.<br /> <br /> A changeling can absolutely get away with full on mortal death and/or permanent Undoing. The Dreaming specifically rejects the Dauntain; the Escheat and the Old Laws\u2122 might be enforced socially or politically, but mystically? The Dreaming wants the Dauntain gone from it, and does not punish those who remove the pestilence. Beyond that? Sweet Jesus, have you looked at Ruin? Smart Kithain wouldn't want to risk a Dauntain anywhere near their free holds for the formalities of a trial, because the one thing the Dauntain are really *really* good at is fucking up Glamour and sources of Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow... Were what you're saying a lie and not 'Word of God', this excerpt would've sound an awful lot, like a racist propaganda piece from a mouth of some Glamour-purist, players could find in a Court or another public Changeling meeting.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You should't feel compassion to them, it's not like they're real Changelings or anything.&quot; &quot;They are broken, unfit to live and pose a danger to society. Killing them is an act of mercy.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> And think about it. If Dreaming wanted them gone, why would it revive them, again and again? Why Brand them in the first place? And as the book says, most of the Changelings get their <i>free out-of-jail card</i>, once they're reborn. It's <i>these</i> folks, that get the short end of the stick. What makes them special? The Dreaming...<br /> <br /> A funny thing, though. The piece on Dauntain says, that they are afflicted with terrible curse, trauma and often a grave unjustice. The Changeling society shuns them. And that they can wield Ruin. Interesting, that it doesn't say they <i>have </i>to use Ruin or particularly prone to evil. They can band together with other Dauntain and hurt Changelings, yes. But do they have to?<br /> <br /> So... a brave Sidhe chevalier with a cold iron dagger comes to your friend, a tormented Dauntain, like you, to murder him without any remorse or regret. Or an angry mob drives you away from your home, because you taint their pretty neighbourhood with your very presence. In fact, they will drive you out of any place, that's even marginally less depressing and soul crushing, than the rest of the world. And one of their butchers will come for you one day, as well.<br /> <br /> You have a choice to band together with other Dauntain. You have a choice to learn Ruin. You have a choice to stand up for the accursed, forsaken and downtrodden. You have a choice to fight back and protect yourself. You have a choice to use Ruin agaist the very Dreaming, that spawned you...<br /> <br /> Would you take it?<br /> <br /> I take it, that Dauntain, as presented, <i>can</i> be a terrible menace, but what you said there sounds a bit extreme and the mindset for treating Dauntain you suggest for Changelings is the very thing, that makes them into a more of a menace, than they are. Dauntain aren't born with the knowledge of Ruin. They don't even know they need it, at first. The Kithain society teaches them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 11-07-2017, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T23:30:09-08:00","id":1156592,"title":"","content":"Now, from what I remember of Autumn People, before, each Dauntain Agenda had their own detailed origin, sometimes an accident, sometimes a choice.<br /> <br /> I figured to suggest and here is as good place as any, to make Dauntain more of boogieman for young Changeling, making them more mysterious or uncertain and to encourage each Storyteller to make up their own Dauntain explanation, based on C20 o\u043a stuff from Autumn People. What is your Changeling campaign is about and what your Changeling troupe would be afraid of the most?<ul><li>Maybe Dauntain are the newly converted Thailain?</li> <li>Maybe they are the &quot;zombies&quot;?</li> <li>Maybe the Dauntain are the unholy mix of Banality and Glamour, a result of monstrous magical experimenting to survive the upcoming Winter?</li> <li>Maybe the Dauntain are actually the famed S\u00edoch\u00e1in? Maybe the S\u00edoch\u00e1in are actually the infamous Dauntain?</li> <li>Maybe they're Dreaming's own servants to punish and police Changelings? Maybe they're the Fomorian curse to torment and punish Kithain?</li> <li>Maybe the Dauntain is what the final stage of Bedlam looks like? Maybe it's what happens to those, who give up to Banality?</li> <li>Maybe they're what happens to those killed with Cold Iron? Or almost killed, their blood and soul being poisoned?</li> <li>Maybe Dauntain is just a catch-all term, that refers to all sorts of outcasts, criminals, Oathbreakers, Thallain and monsters, that lurk in the dark.</li> <li>Are they the worst criminals or the tragic figures? (I always loved the Oath of Undoing of The Cursed Dauntain)</li> <li>Do they know, what they are or are they unwitting slaves of their dark urges? Do they remember their Kithain legacy or think they're human/supernaturals?</li> <li>Are they the new Kith (<i>Autumn Fae</i> or <i>Winter</i> <i>Fae</i>) or can be of any Kith?</li> <li>Are they monsters, through and through or have brighter sides? Are they monsters at all?</li> <li>Are Dauntain curable or incurable?</li> <li>Is being Dauntain a curse at all?..</li> <li>Is what Changeling society knows (or tells) about Dauntain is true? False? A lie? A political piece? Some magically enforced delusion?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 11-07-2017, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T12:55:53-08:00","id":1156774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1156496#post1156496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every story involving a Dauntain is just &quot;how do we stop this objectively evil monster that everyone agrees is a monster&quot;. No moral dilemmas, no trying to figure out who is a Dauntain, just a short battle that goes one of two ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Space was light on that section, and I didn't have nearly the word count I wanted but hopefully there will be more details to expand in possible future supplements. Dauntain are not objectively evil, they're corrupted, broken things being punished for something they did or had done to them long, long ago. In a way, they're mad, not evil. <br /> <br /> Is a Typhoid, with no control over his poisonous dross, evil because he spreads plague? What about the Nihilist who becomes obsessed and shaky the longer he goes without destroying an object or person infused with Glamour? What about the ones who can't sleep soundly and can't harmlessly harvest Glamour? Who can't safely enter the Dreaming? Who loses autonomy if anyone finds their phylactery?<br /> <br /> They're monsters, sure, and changelings recoil from them as anathema, but they're victims too. Not one of them has done anything in their present lives to deserve the suffering. By and large, they're still suffering for the sins of someone else, or the sins they committed so long ago they can no longer remember what they did, or if the judgement was fair.<br /> <br /> I think there's plenty of stories in that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T13:23:31-08:00","id":1156777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1156579#post1156579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow... Were what you're saying a lie and not 'Word of God', this excerpt would've sound an awful lot, like a racist propaganda piece from a mouth of some Glamour-purist, players could find in a Court or another public Changeling meeting.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You should't feel compassion to them, it's not like they're real Changelings or anything.&quot; &quot;They are broken, unfit to live and pose a danger to society. Killing them is an act of mercy.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>No matter how hard you want it, dude, you're not going to change the fact that I did, in fact, work on the book you once accused me of murdering while profiting off the &quot;true fans&quot; backing. Also, not going to change the fact that, as far as Word on High goes, I pretty much am the authority since I rebuilt them this way. Am I saying you can't make your own interpretations? Nope. You definitely can. All my &quot;word on high&quot; intends is to show my thoughts on it, and from what angle I approached the redesign. If I've said anything that makes anyone else think there is only One True Way, I apologize. That was not my intent. <br /> <br /> In short, Firkraag, don't fucking call me a liar or not-nearly-so-sneakily-as-you-thought denigrate me to the level of racist again. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And think about it. If Dreaming wanted them gone, why would it revive them, again and again? Why Brand them in the first place? And as the book says, most of the Changelings get their <i>free out-of-jail card</i>, once they're reborn. It's <i>these</i> folks, that get the short end of the stick. What makes them special? The Dreaming... </div> </div> </div>Because the Dreaming is not infallible and makes mistakes. The write up specifies that too. They should not be, but somehow are. In small words: <i>they were not meant to be reborn. The Brands were to ID them to changelings, which the Dreaming did in their first life. Then the Dreaming fucked up. Now they don't stop being reborn. Now they are not washed clean when they come back. </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A funny thing, though. The piece on Dauntain says, that they are afflicted with terrible curse, trauma and often a grave unjustice. The Changeling society shuns them. And that they can wield Ruin. Interesting, that it doesn't say they <i>have </i>to use Ruin or particularly prone to evil. They can band together with other Dauntain and hurt Changelings, yes. But do they have to?<br /> <br /> -snip- <br /> <br /> I take it, that Dauntain, as presented, <i>can</i> be a terrible menace, but what you said there sounds a bit extreme and the mindset for treating Dauntain you suggest for Changelings is the very thing, that makes them into a more of a menace, than they are. Dauntain aren't born with the knowledge of Ruin. They don't even know they need it, at first. The Kithain society teaches them. </div> </div> </div>It amuses the everliving shit out of me that you get the point so clearly while missing the point entirely. <br /> <br /> PS - if you want someone to, as you said in that same post lambasting me for being the ruination of all that was good and pure in the WoD, leave you alone and no longer engage you on the forums, <i>show them the same fucking common courtesy and don't engage them first</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T13:57:21-08:00","id":1156787,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if Dauntain are a blight only among kithian or do gallians like the nunnehi and menehune have similar cursed individuals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T14:09:41-08:00","id":1156792,"title":"","content":"Yes. My mistake... Engaging you after I expressly asked you no to do this very thing was rather uncalled for.<br /> <br /> I apologize for that.<br /> <br /> I guess it would be for the best, if we'll be done here. Farewell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T14:56:41-08:00","id":1156803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1156787#post1156787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if Dauntain are a blight only among kithian or do gallians like the nunnehi and menehune have similar cursed individuals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they do. Unfortunately, space limitations didn't allow me to get into it. Dauntain, specifically by that descriptor, are largely Kithain.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T06:07:34-08:00","id":1157915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1156258#post1156258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dauntain cannot be rehabilitated as if they're criminals of society. They're monstrous mockeries, damaged by their own ancient choices or with curses inflicted on them. They are, fundamentally, broken. The Dreaming rejects them, and they're fairly twisted because of it. It's not a matter of the Escheat being broken, because the Dreaming does not recognize the Dauntain as belonging to it. They're traumatized, damaged children rejected by the gestational force that should nurture them, and while some of them believe they can be &quot;cured&quot;, none of them ever are and life after life, they come back with that punishment literally branded on them.<br /> <br /> A changeling can absolutely get away with full on mortal death and/or permanent Undoing. The Dreaming specifically rejects the Dauntain; the Escheat and the Old Laws\u2122 might be enforced socially or politically, but mystically? The Dreaming wants the Dauntain gone from it, and does not punish those who remove the pestilence. Beyond that? Sweet Jesus, have you looked at Ruin? Smart Kithain wouldn't want to risk a Dauntain anywhere near their free holds for the formalities of a trial, because the one thing the Dauntain are really *really* good at is fucking up Glamour and sources of Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest: That sounds extremely boring for an ST to work with. Basically, we have creatures with the moral agency of D&amp;D skeletons that our players can just kill on sight and never worry about again. I mean, it does have more dramatic impact if there was a way to redeem them and the Dauthain refuses, rejecting all hope and actually deciding to be evil, instead of being punished for something that might have been &quot;done to them&quot;. Just feels weird that the only way to help victims is to put them out of our misery. Especially in a pretty whimsy game like CtD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T10:08:53-08:00","id":1157956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1157915#post1157915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially in a pretty whimsy game like CtD</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling has elements of whimsy, but it\u2019s still a horror game.<br /> <br /> See also: Stranger Things \ud83d\ude09","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T10:12:03-08:00","id":1157958,"title":"","content":"Sure, but as written this also takes away from the horror. There needs to be either they are hard to identify, are not automatically horrible (even if they almost always are), or something the player could easily see their character turning into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T13:24:41-08:00","id":1157983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1157956#post1157956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changeling has elements of whimsy, but it\u2019s still a horror game.<br /> <br /> See also: Stranger Things \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... no... it's still &quot;A Game of Modern Fantasy&quot;. Horror can be a part of fantasy, but ultimately it's not supposed to be the focus. There was a reason why Changeling was the only WoD game that had a full colour release. Sure, you can play it horror, but it's not like Vampire or Werewolf. Changeling is the whimsy one that has elements of horror.<br /> Secondly: As said above, designated bad guys that can be killed without remorse subtract from horror. Because they remove ambiguity and doubt. There is nothing more horrifying than having innocent blood on your hands or going too far or denying someone redemption. The greatest horror comes when you have to destroy a symbol of innocence to free a raging spirit. Horror is the death of innocence and hope. Without those, you are just killing robots. <br /> Also: Screw Netflix","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T14:55:29-08:00","id":1159573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1156258#post1156258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dauntain cannot be rehabilitated as if they're criminals of society. They're monstrous mockeries, damaged by their own ancient choices or with curses inflicted on them. They are, fundamentally, broken. The Dreaming rejects them, and they're fairly twisted because of it. It's not a matter of the Escheat being broken, because the Dreaming does not recognize the Dauntain as belonging to it. They're traumatized, damaged children rejected by the gestational force that should nurture them, and while some of them believe they can be &quot;cured&quot;, none of them ever are and life after life, they come back with that punishment literally branded on them.<br /> <br /> A changeling can absolutely get away with full on mortal death and/or permanent Undoing. The Dreaming specifically rejects the Dauntain; the Escheat and the Old Laws\u2122 might be enforced socially or politically, but mystically? The Dreaming wants the Dauntain gone from it, and does not punish those who remove the pestilence. Beyond that? Sweet Jesus, have you looked at Ruin? Smart Kithain wouldn't want to risk a Dauntain anywhere near their free holds for the formalities of a trial, because the one thing the Dauntain are really *really* good at is fucking up Glamour and sources of Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep ^^<br /> I did have an idea that a (Changeoing) sorceror using Naming and geas to try and forcibly rehabilitate a Dauntain (a Naming unleashing to explictly try to remove/weaken the Dauntain distinction, geas to undergo Banality reducing quests, such as inspiring mortals).<br /> Not sure if that is too viable, but even if it is doomed to fail, it makes a decent story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T17:32:35-08:00","id":1159633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1159573#post1159573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep ^^<br /> I did have an idea that a (Changeoing) sorceror using Naming and geas to try and forcibly rehabilitate a Dauntain (a Naming unleashing to explictly try to remove/weaken the Dauntain distinction, geas to undergo Banality reducing quests, such as inspiring mortals).<br /> Not sure if that is too viable, but even if it is doomed to fail, it makes a decent story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a straightforward use of Naming 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T03:46:35-08:00","id":1159766,"title":"","content":"There are two key points here:<br /> <br /> 1. The Dreaming doesn't care if you kill Dauntain. In fact, it encourages it.<br /> <br /> 2. A Dauntain, like any changeling, is still half human. While it might be okay to wipe out the fae half of its soul without incurring Banality, the human side of you will still have to deal with the fact you've destroyed a human life too.<br /> <br /> So I don't agree with the argument that you can wantonly kill Dauntain without consequences, and I don't think Maggie was saying that either. She's just pointing out that there aren't mystical consequences. There will still be mortal consequences, not limited to guilt, shame, criminal investigations, distraught family and friends, media coverage, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Arguably, the Dauntain can be used to highlight the disconnect between human and fae society, to create mundane consequences that pull fae characters back into the Autumn World and its own rules, and to create more horror as once-giddy fae find themselves racked with guilt when they realise how their seemingly noble actions have consequences for people in the Autumn World.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Just because one side of your soul says it's okay to kill Dauntain, it doesn't mean the other side of your soul will let you off that easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T05:39:17-08:00","id":1159796,"title":"","content":"I'll point out that in Autumn people, it suggests for each Dauntain Doom a route to redemption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T07:05:03-08:00","id":1159825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1159796#post1159796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll point out that in Autumn people, it suggests for each Dauntain Doom a route to redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think they could be adapted, if you'd like to go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:34:45-08:00","id":1159863,"title":"","content":"but it would probaly be dull for it to happen while securely locked away in the safety of anobles dungeon, to any doom but a typhoid<br /> <br /> If they can end their ghouldom or whatever. I think a nobles dungeon would be a safe place to ensure they dont get more vitae or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T16:31:51-08:00","id":1174148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured#post1153948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wondered a bit, ever since reading the immortal eye trilogy... what happens when a dauntain is brought in chains before the nobility.<br /> <br /> Ideas think they'll be dispatched as a mercy, or given a trial to determine if they can be rehabilitated or not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> According to C20, the term 'Dauntain' is a blanket term for any of the fae who's ways are different or strange to the Kithain. The Thallain, the Hsein, the Nunnehi, the Menehuni, the Dark-Kin, all of them are listed as being Dauntain, even though they behave completely different from one another. So really, it's not a question of if a Dauntain is captured, but rather <i>what kind</i> of Dauntain was captured.<br /> <br /> With the exception of the Thallain, I think the nobles would react in a manner befitting the culture and dreams they've come to personify.<br /> <br /> The Arcadian Sidhe would probably react to them with cultural bias and racism, whether they intended to or not. Central Europe typically viewed tribal and eastern cultures as being ignorant savages. By contrast, the Autumn Sidhe have been living among human society for hundreds of years, and have adapted their way of thinking to suit the changing times. So they might view the Dauntain with a different light than their ancestors would have.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just to give a quick run down:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Thallain</b> = These guys predate the fae. They were created in a time when the Dreaming was pure chaos and revolved around brutal savagery and impulses. They were created by the Fomorians, while the Kithain who came later were made by the Tuatha de Danaan. Most Kithain seem to hate their guts, but the Shadow Court has been known to work with them at times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dark-Kin</b> = Fae spirits who had an adverse effect to the shattering. Instead of being cut off from the Dreaming and trapped in the Autumn World, they were cut off from the Autumn World and trapped within the Dreaming<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nunnehi</b> = The 'faerie' folk of Native American folk lore. They're organized into tribal societies instead of aristocratic houses, and they draw their power from something called Medicine, as opposed to Glamour.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mennehuni</b> = The 'faerie' folk of Hawaii. They survived being cut off from the dreaming by bonding themselves to the spirit world, and now draw their power from nature itself, instead of human dreams.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hsein</b> = The 'faerie' folk of eastern Asia. Their origins and purpose are completely different from their western counterparts. In fact, they're about as different from western fae as the Kuei-Jin are from Kindred.<br /> <br /> <br /> I<b>nanimae</b> = These faerie folk were born from the dreams of nature itself, instead of the minds of humans. So their motives are likely beyond our ability to comprehend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-07-2018, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T17:08:27-08:00","id":1174155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1174148#post1174148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> According to C20, the term 'Dauntain' is a blanket term for any of the fae who's ways are different or strange to the Kithain.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are mixing terms, Gallain is the blanket name for other Fae types and Dauntain is rather specifically different thing. Dauntain in C20 are Kithain, or even Gallain, so horrible cursed and branded by the Dreaming to be actually toxic to Glamour.<br /> <br /> Before C20 some of the Dauntain were cursed others damaged and some were just aligned with the forces of Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T17:33:49-08:00","id":1174161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1174155#post1174155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are mixing terms, Gallain is the blanket name for other Fae types and Dauntain is rather specifically different thing. Dauntain in C20 are Kithain, or even Gallain, so horrible cursed and branded by the Dreaming to be actually toxic to Glamour.<br /> <br /> Before C20 some of the Dauntain were cursed others damaged and some were just aligned with the forces of Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, my mistake then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T17:57:25-08:00","id":1174164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1157915#post1157915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be honest: That sounds extremely boring for an ST to work with. Basically, we have creatures with the moral agency of D&amp;D skeletons that our players can just kill on sight and never worry about again. I mean, it does have more dramatic impact if there was a way to redeem them and the Dauthain refuses, rejecting all hope and actually deciding to be evil, instead of being punished for something that might have been &quot;done to them&quot;. Just feels weird that the only way to help victims is to put them out of our misery. Especially in a pretty whimsy game like CtD</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Going by their description, I like to imagine the Dauntain are changelings who have succumb to nihilism. They no longer believe in anything, because to them, existence is meaningless. It might also explain how they're able to reincarnate themselves. Who cares if you waste this life, or the next, or the next, or the next? As long as you've got your own personal Konami Code, then nothing matters anymore, you've got infinite retries!<br /> <br /> Who cares if your mortal loved ones are killed? They were going to die at some point, anyways, while you would still be walking around centuries after they've rotted to dust!<br /> <br /> Who cares about trying to contribute anything to society if a couple decades later, it's just going to be considered obsolete and replaced with something else?<br /> <br /> For immortal creatures like the fae, the world is on a constant loop. They live, they die, they live again, they die again, and the cycle keeps repeating. What's the point of even trying anymore?<br /> <br /> A creature who is so utterly devoid of hope and ambition would be anathema to the Dreaming and thus rejected by it.<br /> <br /> Their very presence in society invites death to the Dreaming and all those connected to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-07-2018, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T08:43:11-08:00","id":1174877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1174164#post1174164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Going by their description, I like to imagine the Dauntain are changelings who have succumb to nihilism. They no longer believe in anything, because to them, existence is meaningless. It might also explain how they're able to reincarnate themselves. Who cares if you waste this life, or the next, or the next, or the next? As long as you've got your own personal Konami Code, then nothing matters anymore, you've got infinite retries!<br /> <br /> Who cares if your mortal loved ones are killed? They were going to die at some point, anyways, while you would still be walking around centuries after they've rotted to dust!<br /> <br /> Who cares about trying to contribute anything to society if a couple decades later, it's just going to be considered obsolete and replaced with something else?<br /> <br /> For immortal creatures like the fae, the world is on a constant loop. They live, they die, they live again, they die again, and the cycle keeps repeating. What's the point of even trying anymore?<br /> <br /> A creature who is so utterly devoid of hope and ambition would be anathema to the Dreaming and thus rejected by it.<br /> <br /> Their very presence in society invites death to the Dreaming and all those connected to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explaining them doesn't make them any more interesting or appealing. So their're nihilistic and empty. Great. That would also imply that they sit around all day, do nothing and won't resist when someone comes to kill them. Basically, now Changelings are supposed to kill the clinically depressed among them. <br /> That doesn't sound right or fun or interesting. <br /> Really a waste...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T09:25:59-08:00","id":1174886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1174877#post1174877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Explaining them doesn't make them any more interesting or appealing. So their're nihilistic and empty. Great. That would also imply that they sit around all day, do nothing and won't resist when someone comes to kill them. Basically, now Changelings are supposed to kill the clinically depressed among them.<br /> That doesn't sound right or fun or interesting.<br /> Really a waste...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sure, clinically depressed is one direction they could go in. But another direction for those who simply don't care anymore is to cast aside their inhibitions and act upon whatever selfish impulse they feel at the moment. As I said, they basically have infinite retries, which means if a Dauntain chose to become a serial killer, for example, then the state issued death penalty wouldn't be enough to stop them. It might kill their mortal body, sure, but after they reincarnate, you eventually hear stories about &quot;copycat&quot; killers popping up in the news headlines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Are all Dauntain psychopathic hell raisers? Probably not, it seems rather silly to think otherwise.<br /> <br /> But the ones who actually are require a more serious course of action than simply locking them away or killing their current host.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Also want to point out that Changeling, the Dreaming is NOT a whimsical game, as I have come to understand by looking at it from a deeper point of view. It is a game about the <b>death of whimsy</b>, as your character is gradually exposed to the cold harshness of reality and all that it entails. The inevitable loss of innocence, that's the horror that surrounds the game. And anybody who thinks that it's D&amp;D in the modern age is missing the point completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-10-2018, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T10:04:57-08:00","id":1174902,"title":"","content":"In C20 I see the Dauntain as thinking the Dreaming is corrupt and wanting to destroy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T12:20:06-08:00","id":1175253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1174886#post1174886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, clinically depressed is one direction they could go in. But another direction for those who simply don't care anymore is to cast aside their inhibitions and act upon whatever selfish impulse they feel at the moment. As I said, they basically have infinite retries, which means if a Dauntain chose to become a serial killer, for example, then the state issued death penalty wouldn't be enough to stop them. It might kill their mortal body, sure, but after they reincarnate, you eventually hear stories about &quot;copycat&quot; killers popping up in the news headlines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Are all Dauntain psychopathic hell raisers? Probably not, it seems rather silly to think otherwise.<br /> <br /> But the ones who actually are require a more serious course of action than simply locking them away or killing their current host.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Also want to point out that Changeling, the Dreaming is NOT a whimsical game, as I have come to understand by looking at it from a deeper point of view. It is a game about the <b>death of whimsy</b>, as your character is gradually exposed to the cold harshness of reality and all that it entails. The inevitable loss of innocence, that's the horror that surrounds the game. And anybody who thinks that it's D&amp;D in the modern age is missing the point completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reincarnation as a changeling means an almost complete loss of memory until the dreamdance begins and they might be reborn on the other end of the planet, probably surrounded by other changelings. OH GOD, the humanity! That serial killer might... get someone completely different at some point after he has learned how to potty again! AHHHHH! /s<br /> <br /> But at this point, after reading all of C20, I agree. Changeling the Dreaming is indeed a game about the death of whimsy. The CtD I have was holding onto it and loving every moment until it had to go. C20 is about beating it to death while whining that it's no fun anymore. Like with V20, they fucked it up for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T12:31:43-08:00","id":1175256,"title":"","content":"1st ed was a Childling, 2nd ed was a Wilder, C20 is a Grump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T12:56:18-08:00","id":1175262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1175256#post1175256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st ed was a Childling, 2nd ed was a Wilder, C20 is a Grump.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very apt analysis. <br /> Anyways, I'm off, to celebrate the dreamdance and walk into the autumn until winter freezes my smile. (That means that I'll be playing 1st Ed and stop commenting here. No use wasting you guys time)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T19:00:52-08:00","id":1178309,"title":"","content":"Okay, well I went back and gave the C20 version of Dauntains another look through and I think I understand where the Kithain are coming from in regards to their point of view.<br /> <br /> The Dauntain are fae who have been damaged not just physically, but spiritually as well. Their very souls have been scarred as a result of some traumatic experience or forbidden taboo. Because these scars are spiritual, rather than physical, they carry over between reincarnations. You could view the Dauntain as representing legends of people who were just &quot;born evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, it's true that Changelings lose their memories upon their physical death and go off to find a new life, but these memories are not permanently lost. In fact, as soon as they enter the Far Dreaming, they start receiving glimpses of their past lives. And once they enter the Deep Dreaming, they regain their full memories. Whatever happened to make them into Dauntain in the first place, they are eventually going to remember it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But being personally damaged isn't the only thing wrong with them, because Dauntain seem to hold a grudge against the Dreaming for whatever reason and seek to inflict damage upon it and anybody associated with it. I didn't realize this at the time, but one of their possible brands <b>is actually devoted to nihilism, </b>which we talked about earlier. Another brand causes them to spread a magical disease or poison that contaminates the Dreaming wherever they go.<br /> <br /> The Dauntain have been damaged in such a fashion that they have become anathema to the Dreaming and what it stands for. It rejects their existence, even while it is forced to sustain them.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're looking for a silver lining to how the Dauntain are treated, you can always put your faith in the Iron Road, which states that death by cold iron actually purifies the fae's soul and enables them to move to a higher state of existence. So really, perma-killing the Dauntain is an act of mercy, rather than cruelty! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T21:59:05-08:00","id":1178679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1178309#post1178309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, well I went back and gave the C20 version of Dauntains another look through and I think I understand where the Kithain are coming from in regards to their point of view.<br /> <br /> The Dauntain are fae who have been damaged not just physically, but spiritually as well. Their very souls have been scarred as a result of some traumatic experience or forbidden taboo. Because these scars are spiritual, rather than physical, they carry over between reincarnations. You could view the Dauntain as representing legends of people who were just &quot;born evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, it's true that Changelings lose their memories upon their physical death and go off to find a new life, but these memories are not permanently lost. In fact, as soon as they enter the Far Dreaming, they start receiving glimpses of their past lives. And once they enter the Deep Dreaming, they regain their full memories. Whatever happened to make them into Dauntain in the first place, they are eventually going to remember it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But being personally damaged isn't the only thing wrong with them, because Dauntain seem to hold a grudge against the Dreaming for whatever reason and seek to inflict damage upon it and anybody associated with it. I didn't realize this at the time, but one of their possible brands <b>is actually devoted to nihilism, </b>which we talked about earlier. Another brand causes them to spread a magical disease or poison that contaminates the Dreaming wherever they go.<br /> <br /> The Dauntain have been damaged in such a fashion that they have become anathema to the Dreaming and what it stands for. It rejects their existence, even while it is forced to sustain them.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're looking for a silver lining to how the Dauntain are treated, you can always put your faith in the Iron Road, which states that death by cold iron actually purifies the fae's soul and enables them to move to a higher state of existence. So really, perma-killing the Dauntain is an act of mercy, rather than cruelty! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh for goodness sake!<br /> Can you please stop peeing in my mouth and tell me it's gatoratde? So fine, Dautain have the moral complexity of D&amp;D skeletons and destroying their very souls is actually a really nice thing to do because it puts them out of their misery. THAT IS MY ENTIRE PROBLEM! They are BOOOOORING! Might as well just have people being killed by a faulty power line for all the narrative difference it makes. &quot;Born evil&quot; is a cop-out and an admission that you just want intelligent enemies you can bludgenoing to death slowly without feeling remorse. That's what I call &quot;bad writing&quot;! Old CtD wasn't masterful in that regard either, but at least it allowed some creative approaches and Dauthain actually had to do thing instead of spreading magic disease by looking at walls. <br /> This is a hugely missed opportunity and I stay by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T04:32:25-08:00","id":1178721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1178679#post1178679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh for goodness sake!<br /> Can you please stop peeing in my mouth and tell me it's gatoratde? So fine, Dautain have the moral complexity of D&amp;D skeletons and destroying their very souls is actually a really nice thing to do because it puts them out of their misery. THAT IS MY ENTIRE PROBLEM! They are BOOOOORING! Might as well just have people being killed by a faulty power line for all the narrative difference it makes. &quot;Born evil&quot; is a cop-out and an admission that you just want intelligent enemies you can bludgenoing to death slowly without feeling remorse. That's what I call &quot;bad writing&quot;! Old CtD wasn't masterful in that regard either, but at least it allowed some creative approaches and Dauthain actually had to do thing instead of spreading magic disease by looking at walls.<br /> This is a hugely missed opportunity and I stay by that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't exactly say they have the moral complexity of skeletons. Skeletons are (usually) just mindless puppets of whatever necromancer happens to be controlling them at the time. They have no personality or soul of their own, so smashing them to pieces is no different from smashing a doll, except for the likelihood of desecrating somebody's corpse.<br /> <br /> <br /> But even if they are damaged beyond repair, the Dauntain are still living, breathing people with minds of their own. Just because you are severely traumatized does not mean you suddenly stop being a person, and believing otherwise is quite a dangerous view point.<br /> <br /> From what I'm understanding of the situation, the Dauntain are a deadly threat to the Dreaming, and the Fae way of life. Okay, sure, that's enough for them to paint a target on their backs. But what about the Dauntain's presence among the Autumn World, and those not connected with the Dreaming? How do they view the Dauntain? How do the Dauntain view them? The Dreaming may reject them, but it sounds like the Autumn World has welcomed them with open arms. And if Dauntain start going missing, people are going to want to investigate the disappearances, and could possibly mistake those responsible for being involved in some kind of murder cult. The Changelings would certainly appear to be under some kind of mass delusion from an outside perspective, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:27:36-08:00","id":1178753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1178721#post1178721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't exactly say they have the moral complexity of skeletons. Skeletons are (usually) just mindless puppets of whatever necromancer happens to be controlling them at the time. They have no personality or soul of their own, so smashing them to pieces is no different from smashing a doll, except for the likelihood of desecrating somebody's corpse.<br /> <br /> <br /> But even if they are damaged beyond repair, the Dauntain are still living, breathing people with minds of their own. Just because you are severely traumatized does not mean you suddenly stop being a person, and believing otherwise is quite a dangerous view point.<br /> <br /> From what I'm understanding of the situation, the Dauntain are a deadly threat to the Dreaming, and the Fae way of life. Okay, sure, that's enough for them to paint a target on their backs. But what about the Dauntain's presence among the Autumn World, and those not connected with the Dreaming? How do they view the Dauntain? How do the Dauntain view them? The Dreaming may reject them, but it sounds like the Autumn World has welcomed them with open arms. And if Dauntain start going missing, people are going to want to investigate the disappearances, and could possibly mistake those responsible for being involved in some kind of murder cult. The Changelings would certainly appear to be under some kind of mass delusion from an outside perspective, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. And this is just some of the drama that can stem from an encounter with the Dauntain. I could imagine that you could run a very thought-provoking game of consequences, appearances, racism and xenophobia, and how these things pull the dual human-fae soul in multiple directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T08:14:47-08:00","id":1178796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1178721#post1178721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't exactly say they have the moral complexity of skeletons. Skeletons are (usually) just mindless puppets of whatever necromancer happens to be controlling them at the time. They have no personality or soul of their own, so smashing them to pieces is no different from smashing a doll, except for the likelihood of desecrating somebody's corpse.<br /> <br /> <br /> But even if they are damaged beyond repair, the Dauntain are still living, breathing people with minds of their own. Just because you are severely traumatized does not mean you suddenly stop being a person, and believing otherwise is quite a dangerous view point.<br /> <br /> From what I'm understanding of the situation, the Dauntain are a deadly threat to the Dreaming, and the Fae way of life. Okay, sure, that's enough for them to paint a target on their backs. But what about the Dauntain's presence among the Autumn World, and those not connected with the Dreaming? How do they view the Dauntain? How do the Dauntain view them? The Dreaming may reject them, but it sounds like the Autumn World has welcomed them with open arms. And if Dauntain start going missing, people are going to want to investigate the disappearances, and could possibly mistake those responsible for being involved in some kind of murder cult. The Changelings would certainly appear to be under some kind of mass delusion from an outside perspective, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No you don't get it, do you? It's very easy to grab one and beat the chimerical snot out of them until they are undone and their fairy souls go dormant. Then you leave the human behind and deal with the Dauthain's return when it comes back. Just keep an eye on them with Kenning and Soothsay. The mists take care of the rest. No big deal. Everyone has to go alone some time and they won't remember since their Banality is high as heck. Autumn world impact: Some guy sleeps in really long on a weirdly regular basis. No moral qualms. Killing a Chimera has more impact. Changelings die differently from humans. You have to keep that in mind! And no, that's not gaming the system. The Fae know how the Dreaming works.<br /> <br /> If a Dauthan can be reintegrated on the other hand (like they could be in CtD, heck, &quot;The Autumn People&quot; had rules to make your character a Dauthain for a while so you could play a redemption arc) you actually have a conundrum. You want to basically take a person who oozes banality and who might hate the Dreaming and shove as much Glamour back into them as possible. Maybe they fight back. Maybe they go along and screw up your personal quest. Maybe they go along and betray you. Maybe something else happens. But at least you have OPTIONS! Heck, having some incredibly strict politician around, who runs on a platform of getting fiction books out of public libraries and having them take part in a Satyr song contest would make for an amazing session!<br /> <br /> (PS: The Path of Iron is the dumbest thing I have ever seen! Changelings CAN SEE WHAT HAPPENS WHEN THEY DIE! Chimerical death: Mien dissipates and human remains, asleep but alive. Real Death: Human falls over dead, Fae mien remains visible via Kenning and becomes more and more ideal until the darkness itself pulls in back into the body it will reincarnate in. Death by cold iron: The fae mien is visibly torn asunder as it suffers the death of consciousness and the perpetrators get permanent banality every time, while being incapable of filling up their Glamour and remaining in constant pain as long as they keep their weapons. Nobody is that stupid! No, not even Ogres!)<br /> (PPS: To express how I feel right now <a href=\"https://youtu.be/uR0WoO87Qyw?t=4m56s\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/uR0WoO87Qyw?t=4m56s</a> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","user":"Davesknd","date":". 01-24-2018, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:18:29-08:00","id":1178824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1178796#post1178796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No you don't get it, do you? It's very easy to grab one and beat the chimerical snot out of them until they are undone and their fairy souls go dormant. Then you leave the human behind and deal with the Dauthain's return when it comes back. Just keep an eye on them with Kenning and Soothsay. The mists take care of the rest. No big deal. Everyone has to go alone some time and they won't remember since their Banality is high as heck. Autumn world impact: Some guy sleeps in really long on a weirdly regular basis. No moral qualms. Killing a Chimera has more impact. Changelings die differently from humans. You have to keep that in mind! And no, that's not gaming the system. The Fae know how the Dreaming works.<br /> <br /> If a Dauthan can be reintegrated on the other hand (like they could be in CtD, heck, &quot;The Autumn People&quot; had rules to make your character a Dauthain for a while so you could play a redemption arc) you actually have a conundrum. You want to basically take a person who oozes banality and who might hate the Dreaming and shove as much Glamour back into them as possible. Maybe they fight back. Maybe they go along and screw up your personal quest. Maybe they go along and betray you. Maybe something else happens. But at least you have OPTIONS! Heck, having some incredibly strict politician around, who runs on a platform of getting fiction books out of public libraries and having them take part in a Satyr song contest would make for an amazing session!<br /> <br /> (PS: The Path of Iron is the dumbest thing I have ever seen! Changelings CAN SEE WHAT HAPPENS WHEN THEY DIE! Chimerical death: Mien dissipates and human remains, asleep but alive. Real Death: Human falls over dead, Fae mien remains visible via Kenning and becomes more and more ideal until the darkness itself pulls in back into the body it will reincarnate in. Death by cold iron: The fae mien is visibly torn asunder as it suffers the death of consciousness and the perpetrators get permanent banality every time, while being incapable of filling up their Glamour and remaining in constant pain as long as they keep their weapons. Nobody is that stupid! No, not even Ogres!)<br /> (PPS: To express how I feel right now <a href=\"https://youtu.be/uR0WoO87Qyw?t=4m56s\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/uR0WoO87Qyw?t=4m56s</a> )</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You also have to keep in mind that when a faerie soul permanently dies, without killing the physical body, the former host loses all memory of their fae identity. So that Dauntain you just beat the snot out of? Yeah, he's going to wake up to find he's missing a significant gap in time and is probably many miles away from where he was before the Dauntain bonded to him.<br /> <br /> And Chimerical Death doesn't kill the fae soul, it just ejects them from the dreaming and they suffer a bit of amnesia. To truly get rid of them, you have to kill the soul, which involves cold iron, or extremely high levels of Banality.<br /> <br /> As for the Iron Road, I merely brought it up as a suggestion. And it's one that one of the noble houses continues to practice in secret, even though it lead to them being imprisoned for centuries the first time around. Also, forgot to mention that the book describes their murders as being <b>ritualistic</b>, which means they don't just walk up and stab you to death.<br /> <br /> As for not being able to redeem a Dauntain, who's to say you can't? I've seen a bunch of players around here who tell me that the rule books don't have to be followed strictly to the letter, you're free to home brew some stuff if you want. First edition of V:tR, flat out says that some players choose to just ignore the Predator's Taint mechanic entirely, due to its complications.<br /> <br /> <br /> The 20th anniversary books are focused almost entirely around the basic mechanics of the game. It gives you all the rules you need for running a game, but doesn't go into great detail about the fluff material. If you want there to be a way to heal the Dauntain in your game, I don't see any reason why it can't exist. Remember, Changeling is a game about daring to dream, and if conventional wisdom says that something is impossible, then any true Changeling should respond with <i>&quot;challenge accepted!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-24-2018, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T10:00:37-08:00","id":1178846,"title":"","content":"You can't kill a the faerie without killing the Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T10:31:18-08:00","id":1178859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1178824#post1178824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> You also have to keep in mind that when a faerie soul permanently dies, without killing the physical body, the former host loses all memory of their fae identity. So that Dauntain you just beat the snot out of? Yeah, he's going to wake up to find he's missing a significant gap in time and is probably many miles away from where he was before the Dauntain bonded to him.<br /> <br /> And Chimerical Death doesn't kill the fae soul, it just ejects them from the dreaming and they suffer a bit of amnesia. To truly get rid of them, you have to kill the soul, which involves cold iron, or extremely high levels of Banality.<br /> <br /> As for the Iron Road, I merely brought it up as a suggestion. And it's one that one of the noble houses continues to practice in secret, even though it lead to them being imprisoned for centuries the first time around. Also, forgot to mention that the book describes their murders as being <b>ritualistic</b>, which means they don't just walk up and stab you to death.<br /> <br /> As for not being able to redeem a Dauntain, who's to say you can't? I've seen a bunch of players around here who tell me that the rule books don't have to be followed strictly to the letter, you're free to home brew some stuff if you want. First edition of V:tR, flat out says that some players choose to just ignore the Predator's Taint mechanic entirely, due to its complications.<br /> <br /> <br /> The 20th anniversary books are focused almost entirely around the basic mechanics of the game. It gives you all the rules you need for running a game, but doesn't go into great detail about the fluff material. If you want there to be a way to heal the Dauntain in your game, I don't see any reason why it can't exist. Remember, Changeling is a game about daring to dream, and if conventional wisdom says that something is impossible, then any true Changeling should respond with <i>&quot;challenge accepted!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's exactly what I was saying. Fairy soul goes good-night. Human wakes up, can't remember. You Soothsay until it reappears, lather, rinse repeat. With some effort, you can keep the human dominant until the cows come home. If irredeemable, that is the preferred option. (And that's what I meant when I said &quot;mien dissipates&quot;. Because the fairy soul goes dormant and the person is no longer &quot;visible&quot; as a changeling). And you can't cold-iron kill the fairy soul without killing the human. Or did they change that? Because I remember that a death by cold iron kills the human too since, you know, no soul left.<br /> <br /> As for this pearl: &quot;Who says you can't?&quot; <br /> Well, the book, the person who wrote about the Dauthain right in this post here (Quote: &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dauntain cannot be rehabilitated as if they're criminals of society.&quot;)</span></span></span> and you know... I don't discuss my head-canon here. I talk about what is in the rules because it is in the rules. I mean, I have like 5 new Kiths specifically for Alpine Changelings and whole Kingdom for the Mountain Fae. But I don't talk about that because it's not in the book. I don't judge RPG books on rules that I add or refuse to use. I judge the stuff that's on the paper. When a player of mine became a brony and asked if his character could have a chimera that was a &quot;My Little Pony&quot;, my answer was &quot;Unicorn or Pegasus and no canon characters, cause you will visit Ponyville in the future!&quot; (and they did and it was awesome). <br /> But I liked it better when the book gives options to other players to get to play with more interesting ideas than &quot;designated irredeemable EVUL&quot;, like Dauthain have become. And players will not even consider &quot;redeem them&quot; if the book clearly states that redemption is not and never an option. Because we all know how most players are. I see these Dauthain here as a serious step down and honestly, the victim-blaming vibe here is really creepy. And not the good kind of creepy, like you get in Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T14:03:08-08:00","id":1178931,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10243_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10243\" data-vbnamecard=\"10243\">zenten</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13654\" data-vbnamecard=\"13654\">Davesknd</a><br /> <br /> I can't remember the specifics of how it worked, but something in the C20 rules of death mentions how perma-killing the soul of somebody who is in the Dreaming causes the physical body to slip into a deep coma from which they never awaken. And when somebody dies in the dreaming, their physical body (if they have one) is deposited back into the physical world.<br /> <br /> In order for the host body to return to their normal life (if that's even possible) is for the fae inside of them to be Undone, which requires very high levels of Banality. This would be a very time consuming and difficult process for any Changeling to accomplish, since they're literally trying to force Banality onto somebody and doing so at such a level that the Dauntain's spirit completely fades from existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for that quote about the possibility of rehabilitating them, notice how it says &quot;as if they're criminals of society.&quot; Because that's very important thing to notice.<br /> <br /> As we said before, the Dauntain are traumatized individuals, their chrysalis and awakening into the Dreaming was a painful and horrifying experience. They didn't just wake up one day and decide to go on a killing spree of everything related to the faerie folk. They are scared, confused and suffering. It's going to take a hell of a lot more than locking them up in prison and forcing them to perform civic labor to get them to straighten out their behavior. They might very well require therapy, but the last time the Sidhe did any research into the subject, people were getting lobotomized with metal screws!<br /> <br /> <br /> As for your suggestion of just chimerically killing them every time the Dauntain's spirit resurfaces, think about what kind of ramifications that would have upon the host body? If they just randomly start losing gaps in time, or waking up in strange places with no memory of how they got there? Even if we assume the Changelings are waiting in the shadows with a laser pointer aimed at their skulls 24/7, the host is eventually going to suffer from some kind of psychotic break down, which could very well make their Dauntain spirit even worse than it already is.<br /> <br /> <br /> The world has changed, the Dreaming has changed, and even the immortal fae have been forced to change. So is it so hard to imagine that their way of dealing with enemies might change, too?<br /> <br /> Just because nobody's ever done it before, doesn't mean it can't be done. Which, again is what the spirit of the Dreaming is all about, daring to do the impossible. Finding an effective treatment option for the Dauntain could even be made into a quest for a Changeling who's acquired too much permanent Banality and is at risk of becoming Undone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-24-2018, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T08:36:52-08:00","id":1179211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1178931#post1178931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10243_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10243\" data-vbnamecard=\"10243\">zenten</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13654\" data-vbnamecard=\"13654\">Davesknd</a><br /> <br /> I can't remember the specifics of how it worked, but something in the C20 rules of death mentions how perma-killing the soul of somebody who is in the Dreaming causes the physical body to slip into a deep coma from which they never awaken. And when somebody dies in the dreaming, their physical body (if they have one) is deposited back into the physical world.<br /> <br /> In order for the host body to return to their normal life (if that's even possible) is for the fae inside of them to be Undone, which requires very high levels of Banality. This would be a very time consuming and difficult process for any Changeling to accomplish, since they're literally trying to force Banality onto somebody and doing so at such a level that the Dauntain's spirit completely fades from existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for that quote about the possibility of rehabilitating them, notice how it says &quot;as if they're criminals of society.&quot; Because that's very important thing to notice.<br /> <br /> As we said before, the Dauntain are traumatized individuals, their chrysalis and awakening into the Dreaming was a painful and horrifying experience. They didn't just wake up one day and decide to go on a killing spree of everything related to the faerie folk. They are scared, confused and suffering. It's going to take a hell of a lot more than locking them up in prison and forcing them to perform civic labor to get them to straighten out their behavior. They might very well require therapy, but the last time the Sidhe did any research into the subject, people were getting lobotomized with metal screws!<br /> <br /> <br /> As for your suggestion of just chimerically killing them every time the Dauntain's spirit resurfaces, think about what kind of ramifications that would have upon the host body? If they just randomly start losing gaps in time, or waking up in strange places with no memory of how they got there? Even if we assume the Changelings are waiting in the shadows with a laser pointer aimed at their skulls 24/7, the host is eventually going to suffer from some kind of psychotic break down, which could very well make their Dauntain spirit even worse than it already is.<br /> <br /> <br /> The world has changed, the Dreaming has changed, and even the immortal fae have been forced to change. So is it so hard to imagine that their way of dealing with enemies might change, too?<br /> <br /> Just because nobody's ever done it before, doesn't mean it can't be done. Which, again is what the spirit of the Dreaming is all about, daring to do the impossible. Finding an effective treatment option for the Dauntain could even be made into a quest for a Changeling who's acquired too much permanent Banality and is at risk of becoming Undone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, here is the full quote:<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Dauntain cannot be rehabilitated as if they're criminals of society. They're monstrous mockeries, damaged by their own ancient choices or with curses inflicted on them. They are, fundamentally, broken. The Dreaming rejects them, and they're fairly twisted because of it. It's not a matter of the Escheat being broken, because the Dreaming does not recognize the Dauntain as belonging to it. They're traumatized, damaged children rejected by the gestational force that should nurture them, and while some of them believe they can be &quot;cured&quot;, <b>none of them ever are</b> and life after life, they come back with that punishment literally branded on them&quot;<br /> <br /> See? No chance in canon. Every cured Dauthain is a headcanon houserule thing and as I said: I'm not discussing those in a forum that's focused on what is in the book because it's not in the book. I use Dauthain as they were in &quot;The Autumn People&quot;. Because the way they are presented in C20 is disgusting. This fucked up crap should stay in &quot;Beast: The Primordeal&quot;, where I can just ignore it and not end up in a game with a frikking mosaik gryphon on the cover. <br /> <br /> As for my the specificts of death: If your fairy soul dies to cold iron (and it can only die permanently to cold iron. Death in the dreaming ejects you violently and give you tons of banality, but your human body remains intact) the human goes into a permanent and irrevocable coma since it has no soul left. Being a Changeling isn't a symbiosis. You are a person with a fairy soul that can awaken, giving you it's inherit memories, or it's asleep and you're a human who just doesn't remember the truth.<br /> That's why beating a Dauthain into the mists is basically an act of mercy. They just forget but are still the person they were. You said it yourself: The Autumn World doesn't reject them, the Dreaming does, so letting them spend as much time in the mists is the nicest thing you can do to them (if rehabilitation is impossible, which it is in the book). Their banality is so high anyways, they will spend months and years not remembering their fae self and when they do, you beat them into the mists again. Yeah, they lose a few days. A few days of utter anguish and sorrow. The Dreaming is a far greater danger to them than the embrace of Banality, so there is no banal ramifications, since the Dreaming doesn't exist for the banal self. <br /> That's the issue with the writing: They have written the Dauthain into this corner where beating them into the Mists and returning to do that contnuously IS the most humane and kind thing you can do for them. Ant that's why that whole thing is so messed up! You have an irredeemable enemy that can be disposed off without ending a life or causing permanent damage just by giving them an imaginary (and remember: Chimerical things are imaginary to banal people) thrashing from time to time without ramifications. They made them bad adversaries. They are boring now. That is my point. And all you added are things THAT YOU ADDED and therefore not what I care about since IT'S NOT IN THE BOOK! </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T20:12:06-08:00","id":1179414,"title":"","content":"I think Davesknd's point about the dauntain is well made. I remember reading The Autumn People long ago and it seemed really well done. I mean it was depressing but it was supposed to be. At Davesknd's game table and mine, I can see the new dauntain being rather boring by comparison. I'd find a victim who struggled to free themselves but found they were struggling against fatalistic tendencies trained by their trauma to be much more raw, interesting, and frankly true to life. Some people seem to need that sort of no-thinkum villain from time to time though. I imagine that's part of why each game line has something like that.<br /> <br /> However, I think the forum is about a little more than just what's in the book. That would leave it solely in the realm of rules clarifications and nudging each other to recall bits of lore. Those are pretty narrow sorts of discussions. I think at least part of the point of the forums is &quot;So now you have this book... What can you <b>do</b> with it?&quot; There's a point to confining anything too wild to it's own thread (&quot;So... You're running a game using C20 where your PCs are all celtic scions. In the year 2700. Onboard an interstellar generation ship. That's... interesting.&quot; *flees thread swiftly*) but changing the dauntain doesn't seem to rip apart the underpinnings of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23656-lanir","name":"Lanir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T06:10:34-08:00","id":1179502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1179414#post1179414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Davesknd's point about the dauntain is well made. I remember reading The Autumn People long ago and it seemed really well done. I mean it was depressing but it was supposed to be. At Davesknd's game table and mine, I can see the new dauntain being rather boring by comparison. I'd find a victim who struggled to free themselves but found they were struggling against fatalistic tendencies trained by their trauma to be much more raw, interesting, and frankly true to life. Some people seem to need that sort of no-thinkum villain from time to time though. I imagine that's part of why each game line has something like that.<br /> <br /> However, I think the forum is about a little more than just what's in the book. That would leave it solely in the realm of rules clarifications and nudging each other to recall bits of lore. Those are pretty narrow sorts of discussions. I think at least part of the point of the forums is &quot;So now you have this book... What can you <b>do</b> with it?&quot; There's a point to confining anything too wild to it's own thread (&quot;So... You're running a game using C20 where your PCs are all celtic scions. In the year 2700. Onboard an interstellar generation ship. That's... interesting.&quot; *flees thread swiftly*) but changing the dauntain doesn't seem to rip apart the underpinnings of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not saying his point hasn't been made, I'm just saying that if he wants a way to make the Dauntain interesting, he's got plenty of options to choose from. We've already established that they are not mindless skeletons, but sentient individuals with their own thoughts, feelings and lives. The fae might consider them an objective threat, but that doesn't mean killing them on sight is the best way to resolve the situation.<br /> <br /> According to them, the Iron Road should be dismissed because the fae have actually seen what happens to the soul of somebody killed by cold iron. Well, according to the book (which they seem fixated on being established), One of the ancient nobles tells us a different story. They actually spoke with the spirit of their lover, who was killed by an iron weapon and she told him that death by cold iron purified the soul and freed the fae from their worldly connections.<br /> <br /> So there, in the book, we have a story involving how the Iron Road might have some level of merit to it. Despite the evidence piled against them, there are still members of House Beaumayn who continue to explore it's possibilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> Both the player base and even the books themselves support the right to include home brew content. As I said earlier, V:tR openly states that some players just toss out the Predator's Taint mechanic, which seems very strange for a rule book to point out. If you want the Dauntain to be something other than bland, kill on sight villains, you're perfectly free to do something about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-26-2018, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T12:05:09-08:00","id":1182341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1179502#post1179502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to them, the Iron Road should be dismissed because the fae have actually seen what happens to the soul of somebody killed by cold iron. Well, according to the book (which they seem fixated on being established), One of the ancient nobles tells us a different story. They actually spoke with the spirit of their lover, who was killed by an iron weapon and she told him that death by cold iron purified the soul and freed the fae from their worldly connections.<br /> <br /> So there, in the book, we have a story involving how the Iron Road might have some level of merit to it. Despite the evidence piled against them, there are still members of House Beaumayn who continue to explore it's possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, last time I'm gonna be a complete prick to you, but I really feel I have to express my feelings when I read that passage. My first thought was: &quot;Oh, they kept the Celadyr in! That's pretty clever! That little bugger would find a grief-stricken nobleman and morph into his lover to fool them into thinking that annihilating their fellow fairies was a good idea. He is a pretty clever banality chimera...&quot; <br /> Silly me! <br /> There are no banality chimera in this book. Of course not... why put in a really amazing &quot;kill-on-sight&quot; creature like the Frostwyrm when you can euthanize the clinically depressed? At this point, I fully agree that this is a horror game. Reading the book, looking at the new art next to the old one... it's like watching someone you love slowly turn into a Giger-esque abomination just before the Xenomorph jumps out from behind you. <br /> So, you're right. The Iron Path is probably valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T12:21:25-08:00","id":1182348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1182341#post1182341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, last time I'm gonna be a complete prick to you, but I really feel I have to express my feelings when I read that passage. My first thought was: &quot;Oh, they kept the Celadyr in! That's pretty clever! That little bugger would find a grief-stricken nobleman and morph into his lover to fool them into thinking that annihilating their fellow fairies was a good idea. He is a pretty clever banality chimera...&quot;<br /> Silly me!<br /> There are no banality chimera in this book. Of course not... why put in a really amazing &quot;kill-on-sight&quot; creature like the Frostwyrm when you can euthanize the clinically depressed? At this point, I fully agree that this is a horror game. Reading the book, looking at the new art next to the old one... it's like watching someone you love slowly turn into a Giger-esque abomination just before the Xenomorph jumps out from behind you.<br /> So, you're right. The Iron Path is probably valid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never thought you were being a prick. I thought we were having a simple discussion regarding the state of how the Dauntain are treated in game. Also, I don't know what a Celadyr is, V20 and C20 are the only books in the classic World of Darkness I've bought.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T12:50:33-08:00","id":1182357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1153948-what-happens-when-a-dauntain-is-captured?p=1182348#post1182348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I never thought you were being a prick. I thought we were having a simple discussion regarding the state of how the Dauntain are treated in game. Also, I don't know what a Celadyr is, V20 and C20 are the only books in the classic World of Darkness I've bought.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Celdadyr is a banality chimera (yes, they existed. They are beings of glamour that were either corrupted by banality or born from the Changeling's imagination of the coming winter. Their sheer presence drains glamour from the surroundings and they disappear when there is no more to drain. Theyy seek only to bring winter, are self-destructive to an extreme and very rare because of that). Long story short: The Celadyr is a shapeshifter that revels in tricking Changelings into breaking their oaths or abandoning hope. When it finds a vulnerable Changeling, it morphs and plays whatever role necessary to further the coming of winter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}